  "uncertainty_note": "Bands and errors are the plotted values. See the figure caption for confidence level and estimator.",
  "data_note": "Exact numerical artist inputs in plotted units; no values have been digitised from a PDF or recomputed from curves.",
  "caption_latex": "\\textbf{Distributed local feedback reshapes remote correlations.} {(a):} One or three interior detector--actuator pairs in the five-spin weak-end chain. {(b--d):} Endpoint $zz$, $xx$ and $yy$ correlations. One controller acts on site 3; three controllers act independently on sites 2, 3 and 4. Full gain uses $f_j=0.15\\sqrt{\\omega_c}$ at every controlled site; the equal-budget label denotes equal summed squared gain, with $f_j=0.15\\sqrt{\\omega_c/3}$. Independent full-gain drive noise and no-feedback curves distinguish the measured-record contribution. All physical parameters otherwise match Fig.~\\ref{fig:reach}. Solid curves and bands are HOPS with pointwise 95\\% uncertainty. Dashed curves are independent finite-cutoff cavity-SSE means, with separate sampling uncertainty. Neither spin endpoint is actuated. Schematic artwork generated with AI."
